<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 29-day Cetes rate 20.59 in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 29-day Cetes rate 20.59 in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 29-day Cetes rate fell in this week's primary auction and demand fell slightly, Banco de Mexico said.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>29-Day	20.59	    -111	    20.50     20.75</p>
<p>92-Day	21.38	    - 85	    21.17     21.43</p>
<p>183-Day     21.94	    - 79	    21.86     21.98</p>
<p>344-Day     23.44				23.27     23.54</p>
<p>Last week the 350-day paper was assigned at 23.96 pct.  </p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>29-Day	800 million pesos   2.97 bln pesos    3.71</p>
<p>92-Day	800 million pesos   4.80 bln pesos    6.00</p>
<p>183-Day     800 million pesos   5.03 bln pesos    6.29</p>
<p>344-Day     600 million pesos   2.25 bln pesos    3.75</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 5.02 on demand of 15.05 billion pesos compared with 5.02 percent the week before, on demand of 15.07 billion pesos the week before.</p>
<p>Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    29-Day			   16 basis points</p>
<p>    92-Day			    5 basis points</p>
<p>    183-Day			   4 basis points</p>
<p>    344-Day			  10 basis points</p>
<p>((--Dan Trotta, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9507))</p>
</text>
